  "title": "Canada's Euthanasia Ban Extended for Mental Illness",
  "summary": "Canada has indefinitely paused plans for assisted dying for people with mental illness, with the ruling Liberal party seeking to address a growing conflict over access to physician-assisted death.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Canada's federal government has indefinitely suspended plans for assisted dying for people with mental illness.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The legislation aims to address a clash between the Liberal party and the current ruling party.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The ban applies only to individuals whose sole health condition is mental illness, with patients having other conditions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
