  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Canada suspends plans to expand assisted dying to people with mental illness",
      "link": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqd09g0gj50ko?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "description": "People with mental illness alone were to be eligible for assisted dying in Canada in March 2027, but that has now been paused indefinitely.",
      "source_name": "BBC World News",
      "published": "2026-10-07T19:30:51"
    },
    {
      "title": "Canada to indefinitely bar mental illness as sole reason for access to euthanasia",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/07/canada-assisted-dying-mental-illness",
      "description": "<p>Legislation is an effort by ruling Liberals to address growing clash over who has access to doctor-assisted death</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/canada\">Canada</a>’s federal government said on Wednesday it would advance legislation to prevent people whose sole health condition is mental illness from accessing euthanasia, an effort by the ruling Liberal party to address a clash in the country over who has access to physician-assisted death.</p><p>Under the current rules, people whose sole underlying medical condition is a mental illness have been barred from accessing <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/assisted-suicide\">medical assistance in dying</a> (Maid) to end their lives. But that ban – due to be lifted in March – has divided lawmakers over whether to permit this expansion of the Maid program.</p><p><em>In Canada, Crisis Services Canada can be contacted at any time on 1.833.456.4566, or via text on 45645 from 4pm-12am ET. In the US, you can call or text the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline at 988 or chat at 988lifeline.org. In the UK and Ireland, Samaritans can be contacted on freephone 116 123. In Australia, the crisis support service Lifeline is 13 11 14. Other international helplines can be found at <a href=\"http://befrienders.org/\">befrienders.org</a></em></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/07/canada-assisted-dying-mental-illness\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-07T19:00:44"
    },
    {
      "title": "Canada Halts Plan to Allow Medically Assisted Death for the Mentally Ill",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/07/world/canada/canada-medically-assisted-death-mental-illness.html",
      "description": "People who have mental illness alone will not qualify for assisted death, but patients who have other conditions and expect to have a cognitive decline can make an advanced request.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-10-07T19:57:21"
    }
  ]
